#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:2
msgid "COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/include/GENEX_FAMILY.rst:3
msgid ""
"This generator expression belongs to the |genex-family| family. See that "
"section for related generator expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:10
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:12
msgid "$<COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID:language,compiler_ids>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:18
msgid ""
"``1`` when the language used for compilation unit matches ``language`` and "
"CMake's compiler id of the ``language`` compiler matches any one of the "
"comma-separated entries in ``compiler_ids``, otherwise ``0``. This "
"expression is a short form for the combination of "
"``$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:language>`` and ``$<LANG_COMPILER_ID:compiler_ids>``. "
"This expression may be used to specify compile options, compile definitions, "
"and include directories for source files of a particular language and "
"compiler combination in a target. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:26
msgid ""
"add_executable(myapp main.cpp foo.c bar.cpp zot.cu)\n"
"target_compile_definitions(myapp\n"
"  PRIVATE "
"$<$<COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID:CXX,AppleClang,Clang>:COMPILING_CXX_WITH_CLANG>\n"
"          $<$<COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID:CXX,Intel>:COMPILING_CXX_WITH_INTEL>\n"
"          $<$<COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID:C,Clang>:COMPILING_C_WITH_CLANG>\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:35
msgid ""
"This specifies the use of different compile definitions based on both the "
"compiler id and compilation language. This example will have a "
"``COMPILING_CXX_WITH_CLANG`` compile definition when Clang is the CXX "
"compiler, and ``COMPILING_CXX_WITH_INTEL`` when Intel is the CXX compiler. "
"Likewise, when the C compiler is Clang, it will only see the "
"``COMPILING_C_WITH_CLANG`` definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:42
msgid ""
"Without the ``COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID`` generator expression, the same logic "
"would be expressed as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/COMPILE_LANG_AND_ID.rst:45
msgid ""
"target_compile_definitions(myapp\n"
"  PRIVATE $<$<AND:$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>,"
"$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:AppleClang,Clang>>:COMPILING_CXX_WITH_CLANG>\n"
"          $<$<AND:$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>,"
"$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:Intel>>:COMPILING_CXX_WITH_INTEL>\n"
"          $<$<AND:$<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:C>,"
"$<C_COMPILER_ID:Clang>>:COMPILING_C_WITH_CLANG>\n"
")"
msgstr ""
